+# Fetching notes for this corpus
+
+## Hosts
+
+Files were located via GitHub code search (`grep.app`) and fetched raw via
+`raw.githubusercontent.com` — this is stated in the header of `manifest.tsv`:
+
+```
+# repo	branch	path — public CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md files located via GitHub code search (grep.app) on 2026-09-12; fetched raw via raw.githubusercontent.com
+```
+
+No other CDN or mirror host (e.g. jsdelivr, statically) appears anywhere in this
+repository's code, docs, or fetch records. If a mirror was used at some point, it
+left no trace here.
+
+## Rate limit
+
+`GATE1.md` records only a qualitative note: "fetching is rate-limited; the
+remaining entries are fetched incrementally" — 115 of 323 manifest entries were on
+disk at measurement time. No file in this repository states a concrete per-domain
+limit: not visits per window, not the window length, not a cooldown after a
+breach.
+
+I could not find those numbers. Rather than invent a visits/window/cooldown
+figure, this file says so.
